@masthead
  **◈ Northstar / Engineering**

  Internal report · September 2026

@hero eyebrow="Quarterly review / Q3 2026" title="Engineering pulse."
  A quieter platform. A faster release cycle. A look at the systems, shipments, and small improvements that moved us forward.

@grid columns=4
  @metric label="Deployments" value=226 tone=mauve
    ↑ 30.6% vs. previous quarter

  @metric label="Platform uptime" value=99.97% tone=teal
    Above target of 99.95%

  @metric label="Lead time" value=4.2h tone=blue
    ↓ 28% from 5.8 hours

  @metric label="Change failure rate" value=2.1% tone=peach
    ↓ 1.3 pp vs. previous quarter

@panel label="01 / The big picture" title="Executive summary"
  @badge[On track]

  @grid columns=2
    @summary
      Delivery accelerated without trading away reliability. Smaller changes, a shorter CI pipeline, and clearer service ownership helped the team ship 226 production deployments this quarter. The next focus is reducing background-job latency as usage grows.

    @callout tone=teal title="The quarter’s biggest win"
      Build caching cut median pipeline time from 14 minutes to 8 minutes, giving engineers more time for the work that matters.

@panel label="02 / Delivery cadence" title="More frequent, smaller releases"
  @chart title="Production deployments by month, Q2 versus Q3 2026"
    Category  | Q2 2026 | Q3 2026
    --------- | ------- | -------
    Apr / Jul | 48      | 64
    May / Aug | 59      | 76
    Jun / Sep | 66      | 86

  @muted
    Production deployments · Q2: 173 total · Q3: 226 total · Rollbacks excluded.

@panel label="03 / Platform health" title="Service scorecard"
  @badge[4 core services]

  @muted
    Quarterly service metrics. Latency is the 95th percentile; worker latency measures job execution time.

  Service                | Owner          | Uptime | P95 latency | Deploys | Status
  ---------------------- | -------------- | ------ | ----------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------
  **API gateway**        | Platform       | 99.99% | 124 ms      | 72      | @status[● Healthy]
  **Web application**    | Experience     | 99.98% | 218 ms      | 84      | @status[● Healthy]
  **Background workers** | Infrastructure | 99.94% | 842 ms      | 46      | @status(tone=warning)[● Watch latency]
  **Identity**           | Platform       | 99.99% | 96 ms       | 24      | @status[● Healthy]

@grid columns=2
  @panel label="04 / Looking ahead" title="Next quarter’s focus"
    - Split long-running jobs into a dedicated worker pool.
    - Extend deployment safeguards to all core services.
    - Bring median pipeline time below six minutes.

  @panel label="05 / About the numbers" title="Scope & methodology"
    Reporting window: July 1–September 30, 2026. Lead time is the median from merge to production. Platform uptime is measured by an end-to-end availability probe, not an average of service uptime. All data is fictional and provided for demonstration.

